+++ b/artifacts/css-registered-admission-preparation-proposal-v1/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# False-edge admission repair: preserved pending prototype
+
+This overlay applies only to the preserved unaccepted pending prototype after fix138. It is separate from the standalone committed-HEAD candidate. Its selected-value pending mask is also refined by intersection with the existing `find_non_custom_references` result; the prototype's preexisting numeric breadth is preserved, not promoted into the standalone patch. Invalid preparation retains pending ColorScheme demand; pending provider and context preparation remain distinct from Invalid.
+
+This proposal targets false FONT/LH dependency edges from unused fallbacks and selected values rejected by a registered grammar. It generalizes admission across non-universal registrations, alternatives and repetitions. It does not add missing scheduling for direct non-length numeric math. That separate B mechanism remains pending, including the existing 76-case registered-numeric-relative-units lead; it is not counted again or silently accepted here.
+
+The original `find_non_custom_references` function is byte-identical to this variant's original base. Selected var/typed-attribute providers are visited through the existing graph; preparation runs only once every primary visited by that traversal has left its SCC. `lowlink == index` alone is not treated as readiness. Existing provider/custom/attribute links, fallback traversal and cycle poisoning remain. A traversal-local owned result contains Invalid, CSSWide or the actual parsed specified value. It is computed/published only after the existing SCC pop and in-loop early return. Demand/unsettled SCC paths do not publish a prepared value.
+
+The actual `SpecifiedRegisteredValue::parse` handles the complete syntax descriptor, including alternative order and list admission. Namespace argument, URL data, property identity, computational-dependence permission and whole-substitution attr taint match the existing computation path. A successful parse is retained; no shadow grammar or reparsing of a simplified model replaces it. The shared CSS-wide helper retains the original initial/inherited selection and `INHERITS_RESET_STYLE` effect. Substitution primitives and SCC settlement are byte-identical to the captured base.
+
+The generalized collector supplies `SpecifiedValue::context_references() -> Option<ReferenceFlags>`. Supported admitted components/lists provide semantic flags. Unsupported components use flags parsed from the selected substituted tokens, with descriptor-intrinsic COLOR_SCHEME retained. `None` is never treated as an empty mask. The HEAD variant leaves the previous mask unchanged if that conservative selected-token parse itself unexpectedly fails. The live variant retains ContextPreparation demand for such a failure. Valid preparations include intrinsic COLOR_SCHEME even if the collector returns Some(empty), preserving the old descriptor-level requirement conservatively across alternatives.
+
+The only graph update is `value_non_custom_refs &= references`. Thus the local refinement cannot add an edge to its prior mask. This statement concerns a fixed accumulated mask; it is not a proof that all dynamically constructed provider/fallback graphs are globally unchanged. Native WPT and preservation observations must still detect routing changes. Direct numeric math that never entered the original graph retains its prior behavior, including unresolved self-font cases. No numeric self-cycle default is asserted as a normative result.
+
+Invalid selected inputs discard their FONT/LH expression obligations, but retain descriptor intrinsic COLOR_SCHEME: the existing invalid handler can recompute `registration.initial_value` with the current context. It must not be described as always copying a precomputed initial value. Registration initial-value computational-independence requirements justify omitting the rejected expression's relative units; this is not a claim that initial computation reads no context (zoom/color handling remains native). CSSWide copies the existing precomputed initial or parent value through the unchanged helper, with no selected-expression unit obligation.
+
+The pinned 60-row original browser breadth probe calibrates ten direct literal forms, ten unused-fallback failures, ten selected-invalid-fallback failures, and five scalar provider conversions with corresponding fallback failures. Percentage-to-number conversion independently fails its literal calibration and is excluded from that attribution. Noncyclic direct/provider numeric math observations remain B work. Browser expectations for A must be drawn from calibrated false-edge cases plus passing controls; existing B failures should be preserved as separately identified diagnostic observations, not disguised as A acceptance.
+
+Effects audit: captured generic parsing builds an owned specified value using a ParserContext and no computed Context argument; alternative/list parsing uses the real parser. Typed-attribute substitution parses/serializes specified values and does not compute them here. Actual `to_computed_value` stays after SCC settlement. Attr taint, URL data, guards and substitution primitives are retained. This is an API/call-chain audit, not proof of purity of every transitive parser: deeper fresh URL/image source fetches were unavailable, and no claim is made that allocations, caches or other parser-internal effects are absent. Nonnumeric Color/Image/URL/Transform components deliberately use conservative selected-token fallback and require runtime regression gates before acceptance.
+
+The generalized collector changes six files; preparation changes two. `combined-native.patch` and COMBINED-SOURCE-ROLES.json bind all eight paths exactly. Static checks cover forward/reverse/reapply transport in removed scratch, Rust syntax, original prefilter and primitive/helper preservation, unchanged SCC settlement, intrinsic invalid fallback, and intersection shape. They do not establish native type correctness, native refinement, browser validity or accepted bug status. No live source, epoch, Git state, browser or build was modified by this task. The older signed number-only proposals are historical and remain unchanged.
+
+Replay bounded artifact checks with `python3 -I -S -B artifacts/css-registered-admission-preparation-proposal-v1/check.py` and `python3 -I -S -B artifacts/css-registered-admission-preparation-proposal-v1/audit.py`. These do not invoke Mach or a browser.
+
+Independent review: `css-registered-admission-preparation-review-v1`, sealed manifest `f689da7e372e43b5331d46a03b1f616edd134c1454af1fd805df1e65464ce9b3`, found no concrete source blocker. Its bound Lean artifact proves local intersection nonexpansion and a conditional no-new-cycle result for a fixed original graph. It does not prove the dynamic native provider/fallback construction equivalent or close the parser-effect audit.
