+# Independent admission-preparation review
+
+No concrete source blocker found in the pinned head/live proposals. This is a bounded read-only source review, not typechecking, runtime acceptance, or a claim that the whole graph is a subgraph of an earlier execution. REFERENCES.json binds both candidate pairs, original pairs and generalized collector. The owner supplied final candidate hashes and reported transport/format checks; this review independently read the source and checked relevant preservation.
+
+Both original `find_non_custom_references` functions remain exactly unchanged (SOURCE-CHECK.json). The only newly introduced contextual graph update is `value_non_custom_refs &= references`. It cannot add bits to that local accumulator. The live pending Value handler likewise intersects semantic/selected flags with its original selected-substitution prefilter. B's broader direct numeric scheduling remains pending; A must not be described as fixing arbitrary numeric math/provider chains. The accompanying projection Lean artifact proves the local Boolean contract and conditional fixed-graph cycle law, not dynamic-run equivalence.
+
+`visit_value_references` still calls the same graph visitor and maintains lowlink/self-reference behavior. Its additional readiness result checks whether each visited primary remains on the component stack. The cache is created only for non-universal custom declarations after providers settle. The prepared specified value owns its AST, remains local to traversal, and is discarded on non-root lowlink return or cycle removal. Computation/publication happens only after the SCC is popped and found noncyclic. Closed providers are immutable for this resolution pass; this review does not prove arbitrary external mutation or restart semantics.
+
+Invalid, CSS-wide, and admitted values remain separate states. Invalid retains intrinsic COLOR_SCHEME because the existing invalid-value handler can recompute the registered initial value; it is not always a cached copy. Invalid font/line-height expression edges are removed, relying on existing registration initial-value independence requirements. CSS-wide uses the existing copied parent/initial handling, including INHERITS_RESET_STYLE, and does not compute the rejected original expression. The moved CSS-wide matching behavior is unchanged; no new assertion about keyword grammar completeness is inferred.
+
+The admitted parse uses the same syntax descriptor, URL data, None namespaces, AllowComputationallyDependent::Yes, property ID and whole-substitution taint as the original compute path. The original compute path is parse followed by to_computed_value; the proposed cache delays exactly that latter operation. Attribute taint is retained on the computed value. Intrinsic descriptor COLOR_SCHEME is preserved for admitted and unsupported components, including alternatives. Unsupported semantic summaries use selected-substitution token flags; failure to obtain a conservative summary in the head variant preserves the old graph mask. This fallback must never become None=>empty.
+
+The live variant propagates substitution demand distinctly from invalid values, checks selected contextual readiness before computation, and requests intrinsic color-scheme readiness for Invalid when necessary. Pending producer/effect/retry policy remains a prototype obligation; this review does not approve production activation or prove rollback of tracker effects. The Value-specific projection theorem does not automatically cover Invalid/CSS-wide scheduling branches.
+
+Searchfox `PropertyDescriptors::is_universal` was fetched to check the syntax unwrap guard: it returns true when syntax is None, otherwise the descriptor's is_universal. Thus the guarded unwrap is consistent with the current upstream API. The exact source body is captured in searchfox/rule.rs (fetch6c4a12 exit0 after sandbox DNS failure119ee3). This is a body capture, not a claim of a verified revision permalink or local HEAD equality.
+
+Remaining validation obligations: compile both actual configurations; run original/candidate normative WPT; include unsupported typed values and invalid Color initial defaulting so selected-token and intrinsic dependency paths are exercised; preserve original true var/typed-attribute cycle controls; and keep direct numeric scheduling/self-font observations outside A's all-pass gate. Earlier substitution/parsing can observe attributes/environment and accumulate tracker effects sooner. No complete transitive URL/image parser side-effect audit was possible in this review, so early parsing is not asserted pure. There is no evidence here of a concrete URL/image regression, but that broader timing claim remains unproved.
+
+No live native sources, canonical files, Git/index/epoch, build, browser, or ledger were modified. No bug count or formal coverage increment.
